sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title Workflow 2: Traffic burst, full buffer and a dynamic CGI request
    participant C as Clients (burst)
    participant M as Master thread
    participant Q as Shared request buffer<br/>(capacity B)
    participant W as Busy worker
    participant P as CGI child process

    Note over W,P: All N workers are busy, e.g. running long CGI jobs
    W->>P: fork() + exec("spin.cgi?5"), QUERY_STRING set
    C->>M: many new connections arrive at once
    loop until buffer has B requests
        M->>Q: lock, put(conn_fd), signal(not_empty), unlock
    end
    C->>M: one more connection
    M->>Q: lock(mutex)
    Note over M,Q: count == B, so wait(not_full, mutex)<br/>Master sleeps and stops accepting (backpressure).<br/>New clients pile up in the kernel accept backlog.
    P-->>W: CGI output written to client, child exits
    W->>W: waitpid(child), close(conn_fd)
    W->>Q: lock(mutex), get() next request, count--
    W->>Q: signal(not_full), unlock(mutex)
    Q-->>M: master wakes up holding the mutex
    M->>Q: put(conn_fd), signal(not_empty), unlock(mutex)
    M->>M: back to accept()
    Note over C,Q: Queueing delay = t_dequeue - t_arrive.<br/>This is the part that blows up p99 latency during bursts.
